>
>> P.S. gua\spi was much better
>>
>>
> What was the Guaspi rule?
>

It doesnt have a bridi head/tail distinction from which most complicacy
comes:
You say something like
prami mi do
or like
love(you,I)

So it's VSO, or more correctly V O1 O2 O3 ...


> Does there exist a list of the alternative candidate rules for Lojban and
> their pros and cons?
>

fi mi ta broda do - here, probably ta is x4 and do is x5.
Or judging from {mi prami do} a nintadni can think that do is x2.

Also ta might be x1 since nothing fills it so it might be reasonable to
fill vacant slots in order.

One might make a research of which system (as you can see there are
different problems here) is expected more in nature (although which
natlangs have positional case system??? a study of psychological acceptance
of programming languages might be better).

ke'u, I'm not interested in any solutions.
Maybe one should formalize all possible solutions for each independent part
of FA-autorestoration system and other members of BPFK will vote.


